  "slug": "amino-acid-6d41",
  "summary": "New resources and methods expand accessory-genome and surveillance coverage while long-read assemblies resolve complete P. falciparum field genomes.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is resolving pathogen and microbial genome content, from complete assemblies to accessory-genome catalogues. Optimized PacBio HiFi assembly gives near-complete genomes of eight cloned Malian P. falciparum isolates, revealing telomere architecture. NMF applied to 1,398 S. aureus genomes decomposes the accessory pangenome into 24 additive gene modules separating lineage from adaptation and virulence. Resource-level items extend this: proMGE2 catalogues over 16.4 million mobile genetic elements across isolates and MAGs, PHI offers a reproducible Galaxy workflow for prophage identification, host prediction and annotation, and gcPathogen 2.0 expands a multi-omics surveillance database. The items are heterogeneous in organism and scale, but converge on structured, reusable representations of genome variation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
